            'body_en' => "1. The student receives a replacement session, or the session is rescheduled, if it is cancelled or cannot take place because of the platform or the teacher.\n2. The student is compensated if the teacher is more than 20 minutes late without prior notice.\n3. A session is not made up if the student is more than 20 minutes late.\n4. A session is not made up if the student is absent or cancels after the deadline set in the Session Cancellations section.\n5. A session is not made up if the technical problem is on the student's side, such as a weak internet connection, an unprepared device, or inability to join.\n6. If a technical problem on the platform's side is reported immediately and confirmed by the technical team, the student receives a replacement session or the session is rescheduled.\n7. The platform management sets the make-up session time so that it does not conflict with the student's or teacher's schedule, and notifies both. One make-up session is held for each missed session, and it follows the same attendance rules.\n8. Compensation applies only to paid, active subscriptions, and the right lapses when the subscription is cancelled or expires.\n9. The platform reserves the right to review any compensation case and make the final decision fairly for all parties.",
